// One request at a time through the store.
//
// The store's Postgres connection is one conversation: a query sent, its
// rows read. The listener runs each connection as a coroutine on one pool, and
// a coroutine that waits for the database lets another run, which would send
// its own query on the same connection and read the first one's rows. The
// api answered one request at a time before (hale's Server accepted one
// connection and served it), so this was never so. The gate gives that back
// where the store is used: a row's handler and the data plane's handler
// enter it, one at a time, in turn.
//
// The wait is a short sleep, which parks only the waiting coroutine.
locus Gate {
    params { busy: Bool = false; }

    @unbounded
    fn enter() {
        while self.busy { std::time::sleep(1ms); }
        self.busy = true;
    }

    fn leave() { self.busy = false; }
}
